  "site_name": "",
  "description": "Improvements to front garden to create a gravel section suitable to turn vehicles and planting design to enhance overall look. We propose to repair the existing yorkstone driveway section, remove some of the central yorkstone hardstanding and replace with permeable gravel bordered with natural stone setts. Both the existing driveway and the new section will be softened with a low clipped hedge and additional planting. The central pathway will be repaired and relaid, bordered with natural stone with two new york stone curved steps to echo the curves of the building and flanked by 6 native Hawthorne trees in pots. The original yorkstone wall will be repaired and yorkstone coping added to top. The proposal has been engineered to protect the two mature English oak trees on site and the mature shrubs will also be shaped with additional planting added for colour and interest. \nWe have been in communication with Hampstead Garden Suburb Trust who have indicated that the design is in keeping with the surrounding architecture and within suburb guidelines. We have submitted planning and have received preliminary consent from Trust. ",
